<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (On a farm, many different crops grow together. Soybean, corn, and wheat are very common in large fields. Farmers also plant vegetables like lettuce, spinach, tomato, and cucumber. In smaller areas, they grow carrot, onion, garlic, and okra. Some farms produce pumpkin and cassava for local markets. Each plant needs the right soil, water, and care. During the season, farmers check the plants every day to see if they are healthy. These crops are important for food production and for the local economy. Good crop management helps farmers have better results and stronger plants.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
